{"step_index":195,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-08T05:44:36Z","content":"# Phase 2 — Requirements Engineering Deliverable\n## SecureChain — Software Supply Chain Security Platform\n\n**Deliverable File:** [phase2_srs_requirements_table.md](file:///c:/Users/addal/.gemini/antigravity/brain/2ac62f09-2e24-4efd-bd40-62368c77dbf2/phase2_srs_requirements_table.md)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Stakeholders and User Types Identification\n\n| Actor / Stakeholder | Role & Responsibilities | System Justification |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Student (Developer)** | • Registers projects and imports dependency lockfiles (`package-lock.json`, `requirements.txt`).<br>• Runs security scans and models CI/CD build pipelines.<br>• Resolves assigned vulnerability findings and executes remediations. | Primary target learner executing hands-on supply chain security lab workflows. |\n| **Faculty (Instructor)** | • Reviews student project submissions, risk reports, and SBOM exports.<br>• Audits vulnerability findings and lab exercise compliance.<br>• Assigns benchmarks and evaluates remediation performance. | Oversees course evaluation, validates security posture, and grades lab deliverables. |\n| **System Administrator** | • Manages infrastructure uptime, API routes, and user credentials.<br>• Monitors background task execution and database health.<br>• Configures system environment variables and deployment options. | Maintains platform availability, operational stability, and backend infrastructure. |\n| **Security Analyst (AppSec)** | • Configures custom Threat Intelligence feeds and malicious package signatures.<br>• Conducts SLSA provenance audits and SHA-256 artifact verification.<br>• Validates threat detection accuracy for enterprise supply chain security. | Justified expert operational actor modeling enterprise security controls and audit sign-offs. |\n\n---\n\n### 2. Security Requirements Mapping\n\n#### CIA Triad Alignment\n* **Confidentiality (C)**: Sensitive API tokens, credentials, leaked build secrets, and student lab identifiers are protected via TLS encryption and regex log redaction.\n* **Integrity (I)**: Package SHA-256 digests, artifact checksums, dependency manifests, and risk scores are protected against unauthorized tampering.\n* **Availability (A)**: Scan execution runs asynchronously to maintain low API latencies and prevent denial-of-service during heavy scan loads.\n\n#### AAA Controls (Authentication, Authorization, Audit)\n* **Authentication (AuthN)**: JWT token authentication with `bcrypt` password hashing.\n* **Authorization (AuthZ)**: Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) restricting administrative actions (editing threat intel, deleting projects) to Admin & Faculty roles.\n* **Audit (Auditability)**: Append-only event logging for scan triggers, artifact verification attempts, and remediation status updates.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Concise SRS / Requirements Table\n\n> **MoSCoW Prioritization:** **Must Have (M)** | **Should Have (S)** | **Could Have (C)** | **Won't Have (W)**\n\n| Req ID | Requirement Description | Category | Priority | CIA Mapping | Security Control (AuthN / AuthZ / Audit) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **REQ-FR-01** | Register project metadata (Repo URL, Ecosystem, Owner, Team, Default Branch). | Functional | **Must Have** | Integrity | AuthN: Required<br>AuthZ: Student, Admin |\n| **REQ-FR-02** | Import direct & transitive dependency lockfiles (`package-lock.json`, `requirements.txt`). | Functional | **Must Have** | Integrity | AuthN: Required<br>Audit: Dep import logged |\n| **REQ-FR-03** | Detect **Dependency Confusion Attacks** by flagging internal package names resolving to public registries. | Security / Func | **Must Have** | Integrity | Audit: Threat finding logged with evidence |\n| **REQ-FR-04** | Identify **Malicious Packages** by matching dependencies against threat intel feeds (`event-stream`, `xz-utils`). | Security / Func | **Must Have** | Integrity | Audit: Matched intel signature ID logged |\n| **REQ-FR-05** | Detect **Artifact Tampering** by verifying SHA-256 digests against registered baseline digests. | Security / Func | **Must Have** | Integrity | Audit: Mismatch marks artifact `tampered=true` |\n| **REQ-FR-06** | Identify **Build Compromise** by validating SLSA provenance metadata and build logs. | Security / Func | **Should Have** | Integrity | Audit: Provenance missing alert logged |\n| **REQ-FR-07** | Scan build logs for **Secret Leakage** (AWS keys, GitHub PATs, Private Keys, Passwords). | Security / Func | **Must Have** | Confidentiality | Audit: Secret type & snippet logged (redacted) |\n| **REQ-FR-08** | Analyze **Transitive Graph Depth** and alert when dependency graph depth $\\ge 5$. | Security / Func | **Should Have** | Integrity | Audit: Deep dependency IDs recorded |\n| **REQ-FR-09** | Create, assign, and update **Remediation Tasks** through lifecycle states (`Open` $\\rightarrow$ `Resolved`). | Functional | **Must Have** | Integrity | AuthZ: Student, Faculty<br>Audit: Resolution timestamp recorded |\n| **REQ-FR-10** | Generate **CycloneDX v1.4 SBOM** and project Risk Report ($0.0 - 100.0$ score). | Functional | **Must Have** | Confidentiality / Integrity | AuthN: Required<br>Audit: Report generation logged |\n| **REQ-NFR-01** | **Performance**: Complete security scan for 500 dependencies within $< 3\\text{ seconds}$. | Non-Functional | **Should Have** | Availability | N/A |\n| **REQ-NFR-02** | **Transport Security**: Encrypt all client-server communication using TLS 1.3 / HTTPS. | Security / NFR | **Must Have** | Confidentiality | AuthN: TLS handshake verification |\n| **REQ-NFR-03** | **Role-Based Access Control**: Restrict Threat Intel editing to Administrator and Faculty roles. | Security / NFR | **Must Have** | Confidentiality / Integrity | AuthZ: Admin/Faculty role check enforced |\n| **REQ-NFR-04** | **Audit Trail**: Maintain immutable timestamped log entries for all security scan executions. | Security / NFR | **Must Have** | Integrity | Audit: System log event persisted |"}
