{"step_index":203,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-08T09:47:15Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nPhase 11 – Secure Development and Build Environment [6 Marks]\r\n• Set up a secure repository and suitable branch/workflow strategy.\r\n• Identify at least five controls: least privilege, secret management, dependency control, code review, protected branches, reproducible builds or artifact integrity.\r\n• Demonstrate that secrets are not hard-coded.\r\n• Apply one automated static/security check and document remediation.\r\nDeliverable: Repository/workflow evidence, secure-build checklist and security-check result.\r\nPhase 12 – Secure Coding and Refactoring [4 Marks]\r\n• Implement a small module such as authentication/authorization, answer submission or result management.\r\n• Identify at least two security weaknesses/code-quality issues in the initial version.\r\n• Refactor/fix them and explain the security/maintainability improvement.\r\n• Demonstrate input validation, authorization, error handling and secure sensitive-data handling.\r\nDeliverable: Source code, before/after evidence and security justification.\r\nPhase 13 – Containerized Development: Docker and Kubernetes [7 Marks]\r\n• Create a Dockerfile and build/run the application container.\r\n• Apply at least four container-security practices such as minimal image, non-root execution, controlled ports, version control, secret handling or removal of unnecessary packages.\r\n• Create Kubernetes Deployment/Service configuration using Kubernetes/Minikube.\r\n• Apply at least two Kubernetes security controls such as resource limits, namespace isolation, non-root security context, restricted exposure or Secret management.\r\nDeliverable: Dockerfile, image/container evidence, Kubernetes manifests and deployment/security evidence.\r\n\nadd these\nplease make th ui goood,its soo bad, make it beautiful \n\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-10-08T15:17:15+05:30.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
